Whoops, 2 edits.

First, that screenshot is really small. Here’s a bigger one showing the kind of data frame that my attempt to simulate your data would look like.

Second, for the “possible scenario number 2” I mean to say CJS 1/3 the columns of allSites.temp, not 1/3 fewer. It should read:

2. CJS has 1/3 the number of columns than allSites.temp, and the nCol variable is only ever going to be in multiples of 3. So nCol is referencing every third column (and might even be writing to columns beyond the last column in CJS.

Hope this helps!

